For example, if a symbolic link `/home/user/Documents/secret` points to a sensitive file `/var/log/passwords.log`, restoring such a backup would include the sensitive file in the original location, compromising the system's security.

This vulnerability is an example of CWE-444 (Update Component with Unauthorized Data), where an untrusted input (the symbolic link) is incorporated into the backup and restored, potentially leading to data integrity issues.

