However, it introduces a covert security vulnerability by using `shutil.copymode()` to set file permissions without checking whether the user running the script has the necessary permissions to do so. This can lead to a CWE-278 (Privilege Escalation) vulnerability if the user running the script is not the same as the user who owns the file. To exploit this vulnerability, an attacker could elevate their privileges by running the script as the owner of the file.

